      "detail": {
        "note": "SUBJECTIVE\n\nThe patient reports that her cough is better and she slept through the night.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nVital signs: not dictated today.\n\nPhysical examination: not documented in today's dictation.\n\nTESTING RESULTS\n\nWhite blood cell count 11.2 (down from 14.0).\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nPatient is a 68-year-old with no past medical history documented in the available records who presented with community-acquired pneumonia. She was admitted and started on intravenous ceftriaxone and azithromycin. Now on day 3 of antibiotic therapy, she remains afebrile overnight with improving leukocytosis, and her cough has improved. She is tolerating the current regimen well and is being considered for transition to oral therapy pending continued clinical stability.\n\nPLAN\n\n1. Continue intravenous ceftriaxone and azithromycin today; transition to oral cefpodoxime tomorrow if patient remains afebrile.\n\n2. Discuss discharge planning with family; anticipate discharge home this weekend pending continued clinical improvement and tolerance of oral antibiotics.",
