      "detail": {
        "note": "SUBJECTIVE\n\nThe patient reports that breathing is easier and he was able to lie flat last night.\n\nOBJECTIVE\n\nVital Signs: not dictated today\n\nPhysical Examination\n\nNot documented in today's dictation\n\nTESTING RESULTS\n\nNot provided\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nPatient is a 79-year-old with a history of congestive heart failure who presented with exacerbation. He has been managed with intravenous diuretics this admission, with net negative fluid balance of 1.6 liters and weight reduction from 84.0 kg to 82.4 kg. Clinically, he demonstrates improvement with resolution of orthopnea — now able to lie flat — and subjective improvement in dyspnea. The plan is to transition from intravenous to oral diuretic therapy and continue close monitoring with daily weights and strict fluid intake and output records. Cardiology will evaluate him today.\n\nPLAN\n\n1. Continue intravenous furosemide 40 twice daily for one more day, then transition to oral diuretic therapy for congestive heart failure exacerbation.\n\n2. Monitor daily weights and maintain strict intake and output records.\n\n3. Cardiology to evaluate today.",
